Logical: KGDmnDefinitions
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-DMN: DMN File"
Description: "One DMN file as a unit -- the `dmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the l2:decision-support-logic component that points at it and this subgraph name one resource. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/dmn-definitions."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* namespace 0..1 uri "Namespace" "The DMN definitions' namespace."
* label 0..1 string "Label" "The label, as declared."
* source 0..1 string "Source" "Where the node was read from: a repository path or URL."
* sha256 0..1 string "SHA-256" "Hash of the file the node was read from; pins the source."

Logical: KGDmnDecision
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-DMN: DMN Decision"
Description: "A `dmn:decision` -- the question being answered, and the node that carries the link back to the BPMN task invoking it. A file may hold several; the BCG file holds one. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/dmn-decision."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* label 0..1 string "Label" "The label, as declared."
* question 0..1 markdown "Question" "The decision's question, as the DMN states it."
* allowedAnswers 0..1 markdown "Allowed answers" "The decision's allowed answers, as the DMN states them."

Logical: KGDmnDecisionTable
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-DMN: DMN Decision Table"
Description: "The table realising a decision. Separate from dmn-decision because DMN permits other expression kinds -- a literal expression, an invocation -- and collapsing the two would make the graph unable to say which was used. hitPolicy is optional and recorded as null when absent, which it is in the BCG table. DMN's default is UNIQUE, but asserting it here would put words in the author's mouth. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/dmn-decision-table."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* hitPolicy 0..1 string "Hit policy" "The decision table's hitPolicy. Absent when the DMN gives none: DMN's default UNIQUE is not asserted."
* aggregation 0..1 string "Aggregation" "The decision table's aggregation, for a COLLECT hit policy."

Logical: KGDmnInputClause
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-DMN: DMN Input Clause"
Description: "An input column. Its expression text is where data element names are embedded, which is the only reason this is a node rather than a property of the table. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/dmn-input-clause."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* label 0..1 string "Label" "The label, as declared."
* expression 0..1 string "Expression" "The input expression (FEEL or the DAK's convention)."
* typeRef 0..1 string "Type ref" "The input's typeRef."
* ordinal 0..1 unsignedInt "Ordinal" "Position, counted from 0, in the order the source lists it."

Logical: KGDmnOutputClause
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-DMN: DMN Output Clause"
Description: "An output column. The BCG table's four are Care Plan, Guidance displayed to health worker, Annotations and Reference(s). These are column DEFINITIONS in a decision table, not clinical records: no edge from this class reaches an execution artefact, and none may. serialisedAs is outputEntry or annotationEntry -- DMN splits the columns across two element types and the split is positional, so recording it is what lets a rule's cells be matched back to their columns. isReferenceColumn marks the L1 column, found by its description rather than its index. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/dmn-output-clause."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* label 0..1 string "Label" "The label, as declared."
* description 0..1 markdown "Description" "A description, as the source gives it."
* ordinal 0..1 unsignedInt "Ordinal" "Position, counted from 0, in the order the source lists it."
* serialisedAs 0..1 code "Serialised as" "Which DMN element type the column's cells are: outputEntry or annotationEntry. The split is positional, so this is what matches a rule's cells back to their columns."
* serialisedAs from KGDmnEntryKindVS (required)
* isReferenceColumn 0..1 boolean "Is reference column" "Marks the L1 reference column, found by its description rather than its index."

Logical: KGDmnRule
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-DMN: DMN Rule"
Description: "One row. Its input and output cells are carried as properties, not nodes: 250 of them in the BCG table alone, none the target of a cross-model edge. What the rule needs a node for is its citation edge into L1. conditions and outputs are arrays of {clause, description, text}. DMN puts the formal expression in description and the human-readable gloss in text, and both are worth keeping -- the gloss is what a reviewer reads and the expression is what an implementer builds. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/dmn-rule."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* ordinal 0..1 unsignedInt "Ordinal" "Position, counted from 0, in the order the source lists it."
* conditions 0..* BackboneElement "Conditions" "The rule's input entries, by clause."
  * clause 0..1 string "Clause" "The id of the clause (column) the cell belongs to."
  * description 0..1 string "Description" "The cell's formal expression."
  * text 0..1 string "Text" "The cell's human-readable gloss."
* outputs 0..* BackboneElement "Outputs" "The rule's output entries, by clause."
  * clause 0..1 string "Clause" "The id of the clause (column) the cell belongs to."
  * description 0..1 string "Description" "The cell's formal expression."
  * text 0..1 string "Text" "The cell's human-readable gloss."
* annotations 0..* BackboneElement "Annotations" "The rule's annotation entries, by clause."
  * clause 0..1 string "Clause" "The id of the clause (column) the cell belongs to."
  * description 0..1 string "Description" "The cell's formal expression."
  * text 0..1 string "Text" "The cell's human-readable gloss."
